      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nFixes #58680.\r\n\r\nChat `top_logprobs` listed the sampled token twice when that token was already in the top-k, so a request for 3 entries came back as `red, red, here` instead of `red, here, three`. An explicit `max_tokens` that did not fit in `max_model_len - prompt_len` was shortened and returned 200. The Python frontend keeps the token once and rejects the request.\r\n\r\nAn omitted `max_tokens` is still shortened to the remaining context. That matches Python.\r\n\r\n`resolve_max_tokens` is shared, so the native generate path rejects an explicit over-budget `max_tokens` too. Python's non-OpenAI generate path still shortens. I kept the check in that one function rather than adding an OpenAI-only flag.\r\n\r\n\r\nAI assistance was used with `Cursor`. \r\n\r\nThe commit has `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\r\n- `cargo test -p vllm-server chat_logprobs`\r\n- `cargo test -p vllm-text resolve_max_tokens`\r\n\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nClippy finished with no warnings.\r\n\r\n`chat_logprobs`: 3 passed.\r\n`resolve_max_tokens`: 7 passed, including the new rejection and the existing cases that still shorten an omitted `max_tokens`.",
